module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.resolved_reference_outside_execution_closure

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data resolved_reference_outside_execution_closure: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "resolved_reference_outside_execution_closure" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "resolved reference outside the execution closure (an Accepted program contains a resolved call edge whose target declaration's OWNER MODULE is absent from the module closure loaded for that execution, so resolve and typecheck both report success and the program dies at run time. ",

    "MECHANISM: bare-reference resolution consults a declaration population BROADER than the explicit-import closure from which the runtime index is built, so the two phases answer to two different denominators and nothing joins them. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN, found by execution rather than by reading, and recorded here because a class whose only evidence is an argument is not a class: three witness files -- test.claim.spark_serving_observe_witness_test, test.claim.spark_serving_model_store_witness_test and test.claim.spark.spark_cell_role_retirement_witness_test -- CALLED hermetic_fixture_provenance with no import of the module declaring it. ",

    "Resolve accepted them, typecheck accepted them, and every claim reaching the call refused at run time with `no declaration named hermetic_fixture_provenance in this execution's loaded index (searched the modules loaded for this run; the name may be declared in a module this run did not load)`. ",

    "The positive control is exact and cheap: adding the one import admits and executes the UNCHANGED call. ",

    "WHY IT IS NOT ONE OF THE ROWS BESIDE IT, checked rather than assumed. ",

    "It is not `reachability_read_as_occupancy`: nothing here mistook reachability for occupancy, and the declaration is genuinely reachable AND genuinely resolved. ",

    "It is not `identity_absent_graph_traversal`: the declaration exists, has an identity, and that identity is found -- what is absent is the RELATION from the resolved target to the modules the execution loader materializes. ",

    "This is the missing agreement between two denominators, not the occupancy of either one. ",

    "RUNG, SCOPED AND NOT INFLATED: mitigatable at the source-to-witness-execution grain the specimen demonstrates, where the runtime refusal is typed, located and loud. ",

    "THE LANGUAGE-WIDE RUNG IS NOT CLAIMED and the reason is a control that has not been run: place an observable EFFECT before the unloaded call and see whether it executes before the refusal. ",

    "If it does, the class is not mitigatable at that grain without preflight or rollback, because the failure arrives after the program has already acted. ",

    "Until that control answers, this row's rung is a statement about witness execution and nothing wider. ",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed rather than structurally impossible -- source can still omit an import, so the state stays writable, but no Accepted program should contain the edge. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the CAPABILITY: acceptance joins every resolved declaration identity's owner module to the exact local/import/prelude closure used to construct the execution index. ",

    "DISCRIMINATING RED: a bare call with no explicit import is refused BEFORE Accepted, not after. ",

    "POSITIVE CONTROL: adding the exact import admits and executes the unchanged call. ",

    "REPAIR DIRECTION, and the wrong arm is the tempting one: constrain RESOLUTION and ADMISSION. ",

    "Do NOT widen the runtime loader to chase bare-reference edges -- that converts undeclared dependencies into implicit imports and dissolves the direct-import law to make a symptom go away, which is the absorbing-fallback shape applied to a language rule. ",

    "Both phases must consume ONE admitted dependency closure. ",

    "SECOND SPECIMEN, A SECOND INDEX, AND THE REASON IT IS APPENDED HERE RATHER THAN MINTED AS ITS OWN CLASS (found 2026-09-04, import-cut lane, by executing an instrument rather than by reading): the first specimen fails through the DECLARATION index and says `no declaration named X in this execution loaded index`. This one fails through the SERVICE-OPERATION index and says `Unimplemented { what: \"unknown service operation: git.Inspect.HeadCommit\" }`. Different index, different diagnostic, identical mechanism -- so it is one class with two routes, not two classes. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN: gunbc.namespace_cut_subject_observation subject_roster_report refused identically on the wet route and under --dry-run, reached through observe_current_live_hand_rust. The service git.Inspect is declared in module extdeps.git.inspect; the calling module imports extdeps.git -- the SIBLING module in the same directory, which declares no service. Resolution accepted the call, and wet_service_call refused at run time because ctx.indexes.service_ops is built from the loaded module set. Positive control, same shape as the first specimen and equally cheap: adding the one import executes the UNCHANGED call. ",

    "IT IS A POPULATION, NOT AN INSTANCE -- AND THE POPULATION SIZE IS DELIBERATELY NOT CLAIMED HERE. Three members are CONFIRMED by reading their call sites and import lines: gunbc.rust_item_host_observation, gunbc.stage0.stage0_rust_host_observation, and gunbc.live_deploy.candidate. All three import extdeps.git and none imports extdeps.git.inspect -- three independent authors reaching the same wrong sibling, which is what makes the near-miss module name part of the mechanism rather than an anecdote. ",

    "THREE IS A FLOOR, NOT THE CENSUS, and this sentence exists because the row first said otherwise. The confirmed set was produced by a textual scan for a call spelling joined against a top-level import spelling, and such a scan is wrong in BOTH directions: it matches the spelling inside prose and mock declarations, it misses non-top-level and differently-spelled import forms, and it cannot see a module that receives extdeps.git.inspect transitively and legitimately. A second coarse scan surfaced roughly a dozen further candidates, none of which are asserted here as defects, precisely because that scan censuses SHAPES and this row records FACTS. ",

    "The true population is UNDETERMINED pending a resolved-call census that joins each resolved service-operation identity to the module closure its execution index was built from -- which is the instrument the named next-rung trigger produces, and which no grep substitutes for. Writing a confirmed lower bound into this row as though it were the size of the class would make the row a censored estimator about its own subject, and it would later be cited as the size of the class. ",

    "THE AGGRAVATION THIS SPECIMEN ADDS, and it is worse than the refusal: some members of that population do NOT refuse today, which can only mean extdeps.git.inspect reaches their execution index through some OTHER module import line. So whether a service call resolves is decided by a fact stated nowhere near the call site, and it flips when an unrelated author tidies an import they own. The first specimen showed the two denominators DISAGREEING loudly; this one shows them AGREEING BY ACCIDENT, which is the quiet arm of the same defect and is not discoverable by running the program. ",

    "CONSEQUENCE FOR THE REPAIR DIRECTION ALREADY STATED ABOVE: it is unchanged and this specimen strengthens it. The tempting arm here is even cheaper than widening the loader -- add three import lines -- and it is still the absorbing fallback, because it repairs the instances while leaving accidental-agreement intact for every future call site. The named next-rung trigger is what removes the class, and a population-derived execution index would remove the accidental-agreement arm with it. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a green typecheck is not evidence that a call can execute unless the phase that accepted it and the phase that will run it were answering to the same module set; when a name resolves but its module is not imported, ask which denominator each phase used before concluding the reference is sound.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
